# Local CI Gate Before Commit

Before creating a commit, run the checks below and confirm success.

## Gate trigger: code-impacting changes only

Run the **full CI gate** only when staged changes are in directories/files that are actually exercised by the CI commands (`lint`, `typecheck`, `test:*`, `build`, `audit`).

Use **directory-first matching** (not file-extension matching).

Require the full gate if any staged path is in:

- `apps/**`
- `packages/**`
- `e2e/**`
- `infra/**`
- `scripts/**`
- `.github/scripts/**`

Also require the full gate if any staged path is one of these shared root files used by CI scripts:

- `package.json`
- `pnpm-lock.yaml`
- `pnpm-workspace.yaml`
- `turbo.json`

## Non-code changes (full gate not required)

If staged changes are only non-code operational/docs files, skip the full gate.

Typical examples:

- `docs/**`, `README.md`, `*.md`
- `.cursor/**` rule/skill/memory files
- `.github/workflows/**`
- other repo metadata that does not affect shipped runtime code

For these commits, run **targeted validation only** for changed files where applicable (for example: YAML parse for workflow edits, `bash -n` for shell script edits), and report that the full gate was intentionally skipped because no code-impacting paths changed.

## Full gate (default)

When code-impacting files are staged, run this sequence in order:

```bash
pnpm lint && \
pnpm typecheck && \
pnpm test:unit && \
pnpm test:data && \
NODE_ENV=production pnpm build && \
pnpm test:integration && \
pnpm audit --audit-level=high
```

## Enforcement

- If any full-gate command fails, **do not commit**.
- Fix failures first, then rerun the full gate from the start.
- After a full-gate commit, explicitly report that the full gate passed.
- Do not skip the full gate for code-impacting changes because failures are "likely unrelated".
